{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Ben-oni.</b> Son of my suffering." "<b>Binyamin.</b> It appears to me that because he alone was born in the land of Canaan, which is in the south when one comes from Aram Naharayim — as it says ״בַּנֶּגֶב בְּאֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן״ (Numbers 33), ״הָלוֹךְ וְנָסוֹעַ הַנֶּגְבָּה״ (Genesis 12)." "<b>Binyamin.</b> Son of the right hand — the language of ״צָפוֹן וָיָמִין אַתָּה בְּרָאתָם״ (Psalms 89). Therefore it is spelled full [with the vav]."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:11.701058565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}